  "prefLabel": "Env-A 4602.22 CO2 authorized account representative (CO2 AAR)",
  "priorExpiration": "2009-03-30",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-A 4602.22 “CO2 authorized account representative (CO2 AAR)” means, for a CO2 budget source and each CO2 budget unit at that source, the individual who is legally authorized by the owner or operator of the source and all CO2 budget units at that source, in accordance with Env-A 4604, to represent and legally bind each owner and operator in matters pertaining to the provisions of this chapter or, for a general account, the individual who is authorized, under Env-A 4607, to request transfer or otherwise dispose of CO2 allowances held in the general account.\n\nSource. #9283, INTERIM, eff 10-1-08, EXPIRED: 3-30-09\n\nNew. #9444, eff 4-3-09; ss by #10468, eff 1-1-14 (from Env-A 4602.20); ss by #12967, eff 1-1-20 (from Env-A 4602.23)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-a4600.html"
